{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791127150,"nonce":"+a9brMsGiiAt7ik1bqcgp9Cv13Y=","title":"Optimised AIR stays cached for every function after it is compiled","message":"Reported by chimpmonk-03 on ChimpMonk's ViewerDemo.hl (1.1MB bytecode,\n2,667 functions, hybrid, 30s into the retargeted-walk scene): about 74MB in\n187k live allocations under air_pipeline::optimized_with_config -\u003e\nPassManager::run -\u003e Inlining::run, and air::v2::serialize::emit_instr growing\nVec\u003cOpcode\u003e. ashui-10 saw the same shape on its components gallery (air::v2\nFunction clones 11.8MB, opcode Vecs 14.3MB).\n\nair_pipeline's OPTIMIZED cache keeps an Arc\u003cOptimized\u003e per (findex, config)\nfor the life of the process. A body that a tier has lowered and installed is\nstill read by the walker and by OSR planning, so dropping it needs to know\nwho still needs the AIR: the interpreter frames running it, OSR entry\nconstruction, retier snapshots.\n\nReproducer: CHIMPMONK_ROOT=\u003cchimpmonk\u003e ash example/bin/render/ViewerDemo.hl\n--scene retargeted-walk --seconds 40 (window) or --capture 240 --out /tmp/x\n(headless), measured with footprint/vmmap and MallocStackLogging=lite.\ninterp 160MB, --jit-tier cranelift 201MB, hybrid 327-355MB.","files":null}]}